e Note:</b> <b>Gone,</b> are you planning on making seperate &quot;gameline-like&quot; category for Dark Eras sheets on your page? Cause adding a special sheet in each gameline sounds a bit messy. Also you plan on making only those official detailed in Dark Eras and Eras Companion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-04-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T19:19:41-07:00","id":579320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/523870-dark-eras-character-sheets?p=524420#post524420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Firearms is replaced with Archery in some of the older eras, too, and Drive with Ride.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What to do with Neolithic Mage though? 5500 BCE is pre-domestication of Horses (about 4500 BCE), and certainly pre-horseback riding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:04:37-07:00","id":579460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/523870-dark-eras-character-sheets?p=579320#post579320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What to do with Neolithic Mage though? 5500 BCE is pre-domestication of Horses (about 4500 BCE), and certainly pre-horseback riding</div> </div> </div> </div>Using one of left lines for the skill &quot;Running from predators&quot;? Or maybe &quot;Farming&quot; Skill. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Really, in base idea of sheet we leave all the modern skills, even if they are not in Eras - for example, Computers, in very only limited forms, would be only in Cold War Demon and 70s Werewolf - even there, most PCs would not even heard of them.<br /> <br /> But from sheet designing it's easier to add extra lines the players can write the skills they do not have in comapred to modern games than to make every skill editable as we do not know if others skills would not be obsolete with even older Eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-05-2015, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[]